<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-Apr trade surplus rises to $8.3 bln.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-Apr trade surplus rises to $8.3 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's January-April trade surplus rose to $8.3 billion from $7.2 billion in the same period last year, the State Statistics Committee said on Wenesday.</p>
<p>    TRADE VOLUME     ($bln)   Jan-Apr97  Jan-Mar97  Jan-Apr96</p>
<p>Total</p>
<p>    exports			    27.8	 20.8	  n/a</p>
<p>    imports			    19.5	 14.1	  n/a</p>
<p>    trade surplus		   + 8.3	+ 6.7	+ 7.2</p>
<p>Including trade with non-CIS countries</p>
<p>    exports			    21.9	  16.5	  n/a</p>
<p>    imports			    14.5	  10.3	  n/a</p>
<p>    trade surplus		   + 7.4	 + 6.2	+ 5.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
